@startuml
title Multi-Client Chat - Runtime Deployment
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "Server machine" as ServerMachine {
  node "Java 21 Runtime" as ServerRuntime <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "TCPServer-1.0.jar" as ServerJar {
      file "/config/application.properties\nserver.port=3000" as ServerProperties
      file "/css/application.css" as ServerCss
    }
    component "JavaFX Server Dashboard\nServerApplication / ServerController" as Dashboard
    component "ChatServer\naccept loop" as Server
    component "ServerSocket\nListening port: server.port\nDefault: 3000" as Listener
    component "ClientHandler instances\nOne virtual thread per connection\nEach owns an accepted Socket" as Handlers
  }
}

node "Client machine 1" as Machine1 {
  node "Java 21 Runtime" as Runtime1 <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "TCPClient-1.0.jar" as Jar1 {
      file "/config/application.properties\nserver.host=localhost\nserver.port=3000" as Properties1
      file "/css/application.css" as Css1
    }
    component "JavaFX Client\nClientApplication / ClientController" as UI1
    component "ChatClient\nTCP Socket" as Socket1
  }
}

node "Client machine 2" as Machine2 {
  node "Java 21 Runtime" as Runtime2 <<executionEnvironment>> {
    artifact "TCPClient-1.0.jar" as Jar2 {
      file "/config/application.properties\nserver.host=localhost\nserver.port=3000" as Properties2
      file "/css/application.css" as Css2
    }
    component "JavaFX Client\nClientApplication / ClientController" as UI2
    component "ChatClient\nTCP Socket" as Socket2
  }
}

ServerJar ..> Dashboard : launches
Dashboard --> Server : starts / stops
Server ..> ServerProperties : port resolved by ServerConfig
Server --> Listener : listens
Server --> Handlers : creates after accept()
Jar1 ..> UI1 : launches
UI1 --> Socket1 : connection / messages
Jar2 ..> UI2 : launches
UI2 --> Socket2 : connection / messages
Socket1 --> Listener : TCP/IP connect\nconfigured server port (default 3000)
Socket2 --> Listener : TCP/IP connect\nconfigured server port (default 3000)
Socket1 <--> Handlers : TCP/IP text lines\naccepted connection
Socket2 <--> Handlers : TCP/IP text lines\naccepted connection

note bottom of Listener
  ServerSocket accepts connections.
  Chat traffic uses the resulting per-client Sockets.
end note
note bottom of Machine1
  0..N clients; machines may also share one host for testing.
  ClientConfig loads classpath properties when no arguments are given.
  Two arguments (host, port) override the properties.
  On a separate machine, supply the server's IP/hostname;
  localhost refers to the client's own machine.
end note
note bottom of ServerMachine
  JARs include JavaFX classes, CSS and properties.
  Current packaged artifacts target Windows x64 with Java 21 x64.
  The Java runtime is installed separately.
end note
@enduml
